<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n81267" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">περιδίω</span></b>  [<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῖ],</span>
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">περιδείδια</span>
			, <i>to be in great fear for</i>, c. dat., used by <i><span class="en">
				Hom.
			</span></i> only in 3sg.
			impf. and always in tmesi, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">περὶ γὰρ δίε νηυσὶν Ἀχαιῶν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					9.433
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				11.557
			</span></i> : folld. by relat. clause, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">περὶ γὰρ δίε ποιμένι λαῶν, μή τι
					πάθοι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					5.566
				</span></i>
			 : without dat., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">περὶ γὰρ δίε, μή μιν Ἀχαιοὶ . .
					ἕλωρ δηΐοισι λίποιεν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					17.666
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				22.96
			</span></i>.</div>
